# Zone Focus

Zone focus is a street photography technique where you pre-focus your lens to a specific distance so that subjects within that zone are automatically in focus. This eliminates the need to wait for autofocus when shooting fast-moving or unpredictable subjects.

- Set focus to a fixed distance (e.g., 2–3 meters)
- Use a narrower aperture (f/8–f/11) to increase depth of field
- Subjects within the focused zone will be sharp without active autofocus

Commonly paired with AF-C or manual focus for street and candid photography. See [[street-photography]] and [[photography-fundamentals]].
